Description

You are given a string s containing lower case alphabets and 3 integers minSize, maxSize and maxLetters.

You need to find the maximum number of occurrences of any substring under the following rules:

* The number of unique characters in the substring must be ≤ maxLetters.
* The substring size must be between minSize and maxSize inclusive.

Input Format

The first line of the input contains one integer T — the number of test cases.

Then T test cases follow.

The first line of each test case contains a string s.

The second line of each test case contains 3 space-separated integers minSize, maxSize and maxLetters.

Output Format

For each test case, print the answer on a new line.

Constraints

1 ≤ T ≤ 10³

1 ≤ |s| ≤ 10⁵

1 ≤ minSize ≤ maxSize ≤ min(26, s.length())

1 ≤ maxLetters ≤ 26

It is guaranteed that the sum of the lengths of s over all test cases does not exceed 10⁶.

Sample Input 1

1

aababcaab

3 4 2

Sample Output 1

2

Sample Input 2

1

aaaa

3 3 1

Sample Output 2

2

Note

In Sample Input 1:

Substring "aab" occurs 2 times in the original string. It satisfies the conditions:

* 2 unique letters
* length = 3 (between minSize and maxSize)

In Sample Input 2:

Substring "aaa" occurs 2 times in the string. Note that substrings can overlap.



#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
typedef long long ll;
#define endl "\n"   // optional, better to avoid redefining endl

void solve() {
    string s;
    cin>>s;
    int n = s.size();
    int mins,maxs,maxl;
    cin>>mins>>maxs>>maxl;
   
    unordered_map<string,int>ans;

    

    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        string newstr = "";
    unordered_map<char,int> mp;
        for(int j = i; j < min(n, i + mins); j++)
        {
            newstr += s[j];
            mp[s[j]]++;
        }

        if(newstr.size() == mins && mp.size() <= maxl)
        {
            ans[newstr]++;
        }
    }
    int val = 0;
    for(auto it : ans)
    {
        val = max(val,it.second);
    }
    cout<<val<<endl;
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t;
    cin >> t;
    while (t--) {
        solve();
    }

    return 0;
}
